    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34104" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">păthētĭcus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παθητικός</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>full of pathos</i>, <i>affecting</i>,
				<i>pathetic</i> (postclass.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oratio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Macr. S. 4, 2, 5</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">6</span></i>.—Hence, adv.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">păthētĭcē</span></b> , <i>pathetically</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tractare aliquid,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Macr. S. 4, 6</span></i>
			.</div>
